{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceOnH3A","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceOnH3A","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Hecke.InstanceOnH3A","lean:module:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTrace","lean:module:QOU.Shared.MarkovTraceClaim"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceOnH3A.contextH3_has_ordered_pair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceOnH3A.contextH3_has_ordered_pair","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTraceOnH3A.lean#L155-L160","doc":"The witness has two generator indices, so `trace_prod_gen` is satisfiable —\nthe property `contextH2` lacked. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceOnH3A.contextH3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceOnH3A.contextH3","kind":"def","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTraceOnH3A.lean#L137-L153","doc":"**A `MarkovTraceContext` at `n = 3`.**\n\nContrast `QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceH2.contextH2`, whose `cyclic` and\n`trace_prod_gen` are free. Here both carry content, so a result quantified over\n`MarkovTraceContext` is now being tested against a structure where the trace\nsymmetry is a theorem and the pair-product law is an actual computation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceOnH3A.markovTraceH3A","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceOnH3A.markovTraceH3A","kind":"def","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTraceOnH3A.lean#L113-L135","doc":"**A Markov trace on `H₃(q)`**, for any Markov parameter `z`.\n\nA `def`, not an `instance`, for the same reason as at `n = 2`: the class does not\nindex on `z`, so an instance would have to invent one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceOnH3A.traceMap_s0_mul_s1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceOnH3A.traceMap_s0_mul_s1","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTraceOnH3A.lean#L104-L111","doc":"**`tr(σ₀σ₁) = z²`** — the field that is vacuous at `n = 2`. `σ₀σ₁` is\nnormal-form basis vector `e₄`, whose trace weight is `z²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceOnH3A.traceMap_s1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceOnH3A.traceMap_s1","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTraceOnH3A.lean#L99-L102","doc":"`tr(σ₁) = z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceOnH3A.traceMap_s0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceOnH3A.traceMap_s0","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTraceOnH3A.lean#L94-L97","doc":"`tr(σ₀) = z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceOnH3A.traceMap_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceOnH3A.traceMap_one","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTraceOnH3A.lean#L89-L92","doc":"`tr(1) = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceOnH3A.traceMap_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceOnH3A.traceMap_apply","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTraceOnH3A.lean#L86-L87","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceOnH3A.traceMap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.MarkovTraceOnH3A.traceMap","kind":"def","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/MarkovTraceOnH3A.lean#L80-L84","doc":"The Markov trace on `H₃(q)` at parameter `z`, as an `K`-linear functional. ","signatureChunk":0}]}